cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use LARM in academic work, please cite both the software release
  and — once published — the accompanying arXiv preprint.
type: software
title: "LARM: Low Altitude Risk Model"
abstract: >-
  LARM is a deterministic numerical decision-support model for
  low-altitude drone operations. It aggregates weather context,
  building-site geometry, operational context, and equipment health into
  a single risk score (0–100) mapped to one of five risk levels (R0–R4),
  each paired with a recommended decision (GO / CONDITIONAL / NO-GO), a
  buffer ratio, and a completion-probability estimate. The reference
  implementation is calibrated against subtropical (Taiwan) climate
  conditions; region adapters supply alternative calibrations.
authors:
